{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And you shall abandon it.</b> That you not gather from it any fruit for yourself." "<b>And the poor of your people shall eat.</b> Yet afterward it is written: 'for you, and for your servant, and for your maidservant, and for your hired worker, and for your sojourner.' How can both these verses be maintained? Rather, when the fruits are abundant, everyone eats; and when they are scarce — for you, and for your servant, and for your maidservant, and for your hired worker, and for your sojourner. Another interpretation: before the time of elimination arrives, the poor still eliminate them (eat them to depletion), and not the rich."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:58.253819923Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}